# Task 1: Drawing surface and stroke capture

## Goal
A full-screen canvas I can draw on that records every stroke as data
and groups strokes into glyphs.

## Requirements
1. Full-screen canvas that stays sharp on high-resolution screens
   (scale for devicePixelRatio).
2. Use Pointer Events (pointerdown / pointermove / pointerup). Use
   setPointerCapture so strokes don't break if the pen slides off an
   element. Use getCoalescedEvents where available for smoother lines.
3. Set `touch-action: none` on the canvas so drawing never scrolls or
   zooms the page.
4. Record each stroke as a list of Points (x, y, t, pressure).
5. Palm rejection: once a pen input has been seen, ignore touch input
   until the page reloads. Add a small toggle to turn this off.
6. Glyph grouping: when the pen lifts and no new stroke starts within
   500 ms, the current strokes become one finished Glyph. Make the
   500 ms a single named constant I can change.
7. When a glyph finishes, briefly fade its ink to grey so I can see
   the grouping happened.
8. A small debug panel showing: stroke count, point count of the last
   stroke, and the number of finished glyphs.
9. A "Clear" button.

## Out of scope
No recognition, no saving, no templates yet.

## Acceptance checks
- I can draw smoothly on my tablet with no lag or page scrolling.
- Resting my palm while using the pencil doesn't draw.
- Drawing an X (two strokes) quickly produces ONE glyph with 2 strokes.
- Drawing two marks with a pause between produces TWO glyphs.
- Lines look crisp, not blurry.
